NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1119,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,2,3,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.4932,"rank":0.0287,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ018502","role":"top","render":{"description":"A cheerful man suddenly becomes very gloomy and quiet. He assures his wife that nothing is wrong, but remains downcast.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20330","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ098901","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"According to the tramp, a dog that comes at you and snaps at your calves announces a death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ065304","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Later a woman in childbed from the neighbourhood died and the funeral really took place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0483"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ082105","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"If the caul of someone born with a caul is burned straight away, that person is not troubled by visions of the future.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ110101","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is a premonition: later a new house is built on that spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ018502","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"In the end he tells his wife that they are about to lose two children, because he has seen their funeral. Some time later it comes true exactly. The man was born with a caul and can foresee things that are going to happen in the future.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ016802","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He often sees funeral processions pass. The Lord frees him of his second sight, because the boy finds it very hard to bear.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ013201","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In the afternoon a large painting fell upstairs. The glass of the painting and the vases on the mantelpiece broke. It made the same sound they had heard that morning.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ111605","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"She is very upset when she foresees deaths in passing funeral processions. One night, when she has to go out to have a vision, she stumbles. Through the fall she loses her second sight.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ117402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When two magpies sit near the house, visitors are coming.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"WEV001201","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ043710","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When the coffin was carried out of the house, it banged against the wall. This made exactly the same sound they had heard before.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ076509","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is a bad marriage; he is very unhappy, cannot get along with my mother and falls ill. He went about with cancer for years. It was deep poverty.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘man’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0489. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c6"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c6"],"stack":["c1","c6"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1568,"rank":0.3178,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"ZEEUW056","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At night a lady asks a poacher to release her. She takes him to three chests of treasure and sends him to the big black dog to take the key from its mouth. The man sees that the dog is the devil and has himself brought back up, after which he is cursed. He comes home ill and stays ill for a long time. He remains poor all his life.","place":"Zwartenhoek","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":null,"url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38982","original":"Zwarte Dame\nMijn vadere was 'nen perser 1) gelijk da' ge weet. Altijd was hij op zoek naar 't wild, of naar de visch, of naar 't geveugelte, en of dat nou mocht, of dat het nie mocht, daar vriegen die menschen niet naar.\nIn den winter ging hij, als 't gebeurde dat er geen werk was, putters en sijzen en vinken gaan vangen met lijmstokken in het schorre, in den zomer ging hij gaan visschen in alle waters waardat visch in zat, en in t achterjaar en in den winter zette hij stroppen voor de hazen en voor de kernijnen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA004201","role":"member","render":{"description":"Near the church tower a dog stays close to its master out of fear; it howls at a sick person's house until that person has died.","place":"Sondel","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130455","original":"Bakker kaem mei syn jeijen en fiskjen wol folle let thús en wie sa op 'e lette joun, ja, yn 'e nacht faek noch op 'n paed.\nOp in kear hied er jage op 'e Sondeler Leijen. Yn 'e nacht gie er op hûs oan. Syn hountsje Fike wie by him. By de Sondeler toer gie er skean it lân oer nei de Noarderreed, dêr't er wenne en noch wennet. As se sa ûnderweis wiene doarme Fike by him wei, mar doe't hja dêr by de toer wiene, wie Fike net by him wei to slaen. De houn roun deun tsjin him oan, sadat Bakker hast gjin foet forsette koe. \nBakker treau de houn by him wei en sei: hwat is der, hwat skeelt der oan. Hy koe de houn net ôfwarre; hy roun him sahwat tusken de skonken. Hwat wie der, hwat hat Fike sjoen, sa freget Bakker him ôf. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA001605","role":"member","render":{"description":"A few days after a dog sits howling beside its master, the man dies.","place":"Sintjohannesga","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130282","original":"Van der Wal syn oer-pake wie even nei de wetterfloed fan 1825 yn 'e feanderij yn it Skar ûnder Sint Jehannesgea. Dat wie yn de tiid dat der in greate stjerte wie, dat kaem mûlk fan it séwetter. Doe't er dêr yn it Skar wie mei syn houn, roun dy hieltyd foar him út en gong dan wer jammerdearlik foar him sitten to janken. Hy tocht, hwat skeelt dy houn, mar it bist wist fan gjin ophâlden en gûlde mar troch.\nTrije dagen letter wie de âld man dea.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"BIJLSMA004903","role":"member","render":{"description":"The eerie howling of a dog means that someone will die.","place":"Langweer","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130518","original":"To Eastergea by it klokhús stie alear de herberch \"Hof van Holland\". Der binne letter fjouwer wenten fan makke, dy 't der noch steane. Dêr wenne Jelle de Vries, dy hie in houn, dy koe alderôfgryslik spoekgûle. Dan gie der stéfêst immen dea. Op in kear wie it alhiel mâl hoe 't de houn gûlde. Daliks neielkoar kamen der yn dat lytse doarpke fjouwer to forstjerren.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Zwartenhoek belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1137,"rank":0.1967,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ045808","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Children's screaming is heard by the water. It is an omen: later two children are narrowly saved from drowning.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24335","original":"Der ha froeger twa bern fan Simen Spinder yn 't Fliet sitten. Dy binne omtrint forsûpt. Simen hat se noch kret op 'e tiid ret. Fan tofoaren ha se dy bern dêr razen heard. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ027603","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Two brothers were once out hunting polecats when one of them saw a coffin with a white cloth. The other saw nothing. A white cloth over a coffin meant that the person had died in childbirth.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0483","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21630","original":"Ek in kear, doe wienen wy der wer togearre op út to murdejeijen. Wy wienen achter it Dwarsdjip.\n\"Sjoch\", sei Wessel ynienen.\n\"Hwat sjochstû\", sei 'k.\n\"In kiste mei in wyt kleed der oer\", sei er.\nDan wie der ien yn 'e kream stoarn as der in wyt kleed oer de kiste lei.\n\"Ik sjoch neat\", sei 'k.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ017911","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Two people step aside for a funeral procession; a short time later someone actually dies.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20224","original":"Ik en Wibe Weening hienen op in joun yn 'e Harkema oan 't kuijerjen west. Doe sei Wibe tsjin my: \"Mast even út 'e wei gean.\" Wy stienen in skoftsje oan 'e kant fan 'e wei. \"Nou kinne wy wol wer op 'e wei\", sei er. Hy hie in lykstaesje foarbygean sjoen. Mar ik seach neat. 't Wie Pytsje Alma har man, dêr't er de bigraffenis fan sjoen hie. Dy is koart dêrnei stoarn.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","2 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":2},"on_success":{"chime":2,"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.9161,"rank":0.8022,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST276","role":"card","render":{"description":"The stiepelteken (mark in the doorpost) came about when a wit wief (white woman) threw the axe with which she was chasing a farmhand, and it landed in the doorpost of the barn door. The farmhand had challenged the witte wieven (white women) by bringing a spit to a spinning gathering and immediately running off again.","place":"Vasse","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"B.J.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13620","original":"Op veel plaatsen in Twente hoort men de volgende vertellingen.\nDe Witte Wiefkes hadden eens gasten of spinvisite. De knecht van een boer uit de buurt bracht er het spit heen; en toen als de wind weer terug naar huis te paard. Maar een der witte wiefkes zat hem met een bijl achterna. De knecht was echter eerder thuis. Zij wierp hem echter met de bijl na, die in den stipel (deurstijl achterdeur) bleef zitten en toen riep ze nog: \"Had ik mien eenen schoen zo gauw knupt als m'andren rupt, dan was doe 't gebraad west.\"","lang":"Standard Dutch; Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST280","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand walks past the Witte Wieven (white women) at night. Because he insults them, one of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost).","place":"Goor","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"J.W.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13624","original":"Witte Wieven waren hier bekend. Men geloofde dat ze ongeluk aanbrachten.\nEen verhaal gaat hier, dat een boerenzoon laat naat huis terugkeerde en langs een plek kwam, waar een wit wief een gebraad aan het spit ronddraaide. De boerenzoon beledigde haar, waarna het witte wief hem met een bijl achterna zette. Gelukkig voor de boerenzoon kon hij nog net de boerderij bereiken, voor het witte wief hem had ingehaald. Maar deze gooide hem nog de bijl achterna, die in de \"stiepel\" bleef zitten.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_13_014","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man who brings the spit to the hill of the Huns is then chased by a Hun with an axe. The man manages to get into the farmhouse; the Hun throws the axe after him, and it lands in the doorpost.","place":"Rossum","prov":"Ov.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128541","original":"Spit brengen\nG.M.: Ja dee knecht van Scholtn möt dat doan hebn, den hef t spit doar op n Huunboarg bracht en den hef t peard bie zik had en tenminste zoa heb ik t wa es heurd verteln en doe hef he t spit hef he doar henbracht noa n Huunboarg en doe is het der tuskn oet goan, n Huun löaw’k noa met t haandbiel en doe is Schoolt zien knecht bie t Schoolt owwer n onderstn nienduur vlögn en doe hef n Huun hem nog noasmetn en t haandbielkn in in duurnpost smetn\nE.M.: Dat heb ik ok vaak heurd.\nG.M.: Zoa heb ik t vaak heurn verteln.\nE.M.: A’j dat oppervlakkig bekiekt, zo’j zegn. Dat kan hoast geelsnich, mer ja ik heb wa honderd moal heurn verteln.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with A. 3 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"0eec280b8b12db04","accepted_hashes":["1349d053bb1bd4e9128385509a6d42e79a03bf0136880c9880af5b432264fc69","8e19ace9aeaa27867453c9ba3267ed1a3fb99fddf2f9ef68926b04439b1ed3ca","d6a8ad2772b7906c6cb2f93ff650c3689ad0082e65f88e873f692d2ea858b772"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0633,"rank":0.4745,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0296","role":"member","render":{"description":"White ladies haunted 't Slot. Many people did not dare to go near it because of them.","place":"Tienhoven","prov":"Utr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50997","original":"Bij 't Slot* spookte 't altijd. D'r liepen dames in het wit. Een hoop mensen, die d'r niet heen dorsten.\n\n*Ameide","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ053309","role":"member","render":{"description":"One night a man suddenly sees two white women. The two women sit down on his cart. The man becomes so frightened that he quickly runs off.","place":"Ons Belang","prov":"Utr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25339","original":"Hjir ien út 'e Harkema ried us mei de boerewein op in nacht nei Readskuorre ta. Doe seach er dêr ynienen twa wite froulju foar him. Hy ried dêr mei de hynders lyk op yn.\nDoe kommen dy beide froulju yn 't wyt by him op 'e wein.\nHy woarde sa binaud, dat hy sette sokken en naeide út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1499","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"We used to have a neighbour of whom it was said that he could turn into a werewolf. People were afraid of him.","place":"Herwijnen","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125634","original":"Heel vroeger woonde d'r een buurman naast ons. Die kwam van Kuilenburg. Toen ging die naar Waardenburg. Daar wier gezeed, dat ie kon weerwolve. Die ken weerwolve. Hij stond d'r voor bekend in Waardenburg. De jongens rende d'r voorbij.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ063612","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Almelo they have witte wijven (white women) and a beautiful woman haunts the place. I heard that when I was buying horses there.","place":"Soesterberg","prov":"Utr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27090","original":"In Almelo hebben ze witte wiven. En daar spookt ook nog een mooie vrouw om. Ik heb het daar wel eens gehoord toen ik daar peerden kocht.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Herwijnen belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0353,"rank":0.4407,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"ZEEUW051","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Grauw it sometimes happened, if you went out late in the evening, that the Witte Juffer (White Lady) kept you company.","place":"Graauw","prov":"Zl.","year":1921,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38977","original":"Witte Juffers\n\nOp Grauw gebeurde het soms, als ge 's avonds laat op pad ging, dat ge gezelschap kreegt van de Witte Juffer.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"TINNEV038","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man makes a bet that he dares to ask the wit wief (white woman) from the woods to dance. They dance until the man can go on no longer and drops dead.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22384","original":"25. DE WITTE WIEF VAN MONTFELAND\nIen de bös rond Montfeland zitte witte wief die gin mins kwaod doen, ai eur teminste met rös laot. \nIemand uut Beak, dén met 'n zatte kop aan zon wief vroeg of ze met um wol danse, kosse die vroag 't lève. Zi'j bleef de hele nach met um aan 't deurdanse. De man wol iedere kier opholle, mao dat \nging niet. Hi'j mos deurdrèje, ook toe te nie meer kon. 't Zweit liep um nèven 't lief as offe ien de bare zon aan 't rogmèje was. Hi'j smeken um toch op te holle, mor 't wief ging deur. Endelijk, ien de margetied, viel de man dood veur eur vuut neer. …","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_08A_001","role":"card","render":{"description":"Dwelling place of witte wieven (white women); they are helpful, and if left alone they do nothing.","place":"Mander","prov":"Ov.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128452","original":"Bels: Doar hebt ze ok wat vuindn, nich, doe ze doar vrower an 't bouwn warn west, nich, en an 't eand har der dan nen kôm koffie of melk, dee har der kloar stoan zoa vertöln ze van oolds oet, nich.\nIk: Woar hebt dee witte wiew dan eigenlik in lewd dan?\nB: Dee hebt in de holn lewd.\nIk: Was dat een of andre beult, woar at ze inzatn?\nB: Joa ze zatn in ne beult, dat warn twee beultn, dee hebt ze later nog ôpgrövn, dokter Hijszeler is der wa met an 't grewn west met dee beultn, nich? …","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"WEV014306","role":"card","render":{"description":"Nobody dares to buy a house in which witte juffers (white ladies) walk.","place":"Meerland","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44759","original":"Bie Appingedam ston eerder n hoes, woor t in spookde.\nZai zaggen er widde juffers in loopn.\nEt is n poar keer te koop aanboden, moar gainaine dus t koopn. \nHou of t er loater mit goan is, wait ik nait.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c5","word":"three","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.1399,"rank":0.219,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN009612","role":"target","render":{"description":"Werewolf makes itself carried; a girl is said to be able to turn into a werewolf.","place":null,"prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208996","original":"Weerwolf . \"Oom Toon\" had de weerwolf gezien. Hij zag eruit als een half kaalgeschoren hond. Twee keer had hij hem moeten dragen tot waar de huizen van Putbroek stonden. In Montfort zou een meisje zich in een weerwolf hebben kunnen veranderen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LINSSEN001602","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Someone fears the werewolf will jump on his back, and while running away he hears his own trouser legs rubbing together, which sounds like a call to catch him. It earned him the nickname Frans Vattem.","place":"Maasbracht","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208281","original":"Weerwolf. Een eenvoudige landbouwer in de Brachter beek was nogal angstig aangelegd. Hij meende dat de weerwolf hem op de hielen had gezeten. Op een avond was hij op weg geweest op een vrij eenzaam pad tussen Brachterbeek en Maasbracht, toen hij opeens achter zich hoorde:\"Vat hem\", \"Vat hem\" Hoe sneller hij liep, hoe vlugger de roep. Bij de Mispadenhof gekomen sprong hem de weerwolf op de rug. Hoe dat verder gegaan was vermeldt de geschiedenis niet. Wel weet men een verklaring te geven van de stem die hij hoorde. Hij droeg namelijk een Manchester broek met ribbels. Hoe sneller hij liep, hoe vaker de broekspijpen langs elkaar schuurden, hoe sneller en hoe sneller de roep: \"Vat hem\". \nHij heeft later de naam Frans Vattem gehouden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1","geo":[51.13929,5.88627]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN005701","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Werewolf tries to jump on a woman's back, disappears after screaming.","place":"Wessem","prov":"L.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208582","original":"Weerwolf: Bij Stèveke, een wessemer inwoner, lag voor het huis een grote vierkante steen. Daarachter zat op zekere avond een weerwolf verborgen. Een vrouw die daar passeerde, schrok plotseling toen het ondier op haar afkwam en haar op de nek sprong. Zij holde uit alle macht weg in de richting van de Steenweg. Daar stond juist de \"kromme boer\", leunende op de benedenste helft van een in tweeën gedeelde staldeur. Hij liet een schreeuw, de weerwolf voelde zich bedreigd en verdween in de duisternis.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1","geo":[51.15954,5.88146]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN007303","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Seeing lights, probably the eyes of a werewolf, because a man has to carry the werewolf for a while.","place":"Melick","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208780","original":"Dwaallichten: Een man uit Broeksittard, later wonende te Melick, ging 's avonds vaak naar Roermond, naar Kapel in het Zand. Van daaruit nam hij een binnenweg naar Melick toe. Op zekere avond zag hij in het donker twee scherpe lichten, die hij dan links dan rechts van de weg zag. Op een gegeven moment waren zij verdwenen. Maar hij voelde plotseling een last op zijn rug. Zijn borst werd omklemd door een paar armen of poten. Bij het dorp werd hij losge;aten. Hij had de weerwolf gedragen. De lichten waren waarschijnlijk de glinsterende ogen van de weerwolf geweest.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1","geo":[51.15917,6.01667]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Melick.","Find Putbroek on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[51.09667,5.9875],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Putbroek"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2646,"rank":0.814,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ084112","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven girls is a nightmare and one of seven boys is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32830","original":"Se sizze fan 'e sawn famkes út ien húshâlding is ien in nachtmerje en fan 'e sawn jonges út in húshâlding is ien in wearwolf","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002419","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Appearance and doings of werewolves.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210126","original":"Dirk Winsen vertelde: \"Hij ister vannach weer gewes\" Hij was een weerwolf. Weerwolven liepen \"op-te-vier\" nl. op handen en voeten. Men kon dit aan hun vingers zien, want ze hadden \"zwil (= eelt) opte kneukels\" (= gewrichten). Ze hadden een \"vel\" om, dat ze ergens vandaan haalden. Waarvandaan wist R. niet. Ze lieten een brommend geluid horen en hadden vurige ogen. Om twaalf uur moesten ze er op uit om te gaan \"wèrwolve\". Hun lichaam mocht dan nog wel op het bed liggen, maar de geest was er uit, die was bezig het de mensen lastig te maken, Ze liepen de late wandelaars voor de voeten, gooiden mensen met kar en paard van de dijk, maar wat een geluk was: er bleek na deze behandeling niets gebroken. Plotseling kwamen de weerwolven tegen de dijk op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ101519","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven daughters is a nightmare; one of seven sons is a werewolf.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36981","original":"Ien fan sawn famkes út ien gesin wie in nachtmerje.\nIen fan sawn jonges út ien gesin wie in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ085401","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. When he has one of his fits, you must throw him an old apron or something like it. He then tears it to pieces. If you see someone with threads hanging from his mouth, you can be sure he is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33002","original":"In wearwolf is in minske, dy forropt de boel. 't Is ien fan sawn jonges (7 bruorren). As er wer sa'n kuer krijt, dat er hwat forskuorre mat, mat men him in âld skelk of sahwathinne tasmite. Us mem sei, dan gebeurde 't wol dat him even letter de triedden ta de mûle úthongen.\nAs men sa'n ien seach, dy't triedden ta de mûle út hie, koe men der fan op oan dat it in wearwolf wie. Dêr koe men se oan herkenne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Opheusden belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0756,"rank":0.6667,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ096724","role":"door","render":{"description":"One in seven brothers is a werewolf. Werewolves tear apart and kill everything they come across. So you must throw him something, such as a cloth or a ball, that he can sink his teeth into.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36156","original":"In wearwolf is in man dy't alles forskuort. Ien fan sawn bruorren dy't op elkoar folgje is in wearwolf. De wearwolf makket alles dea as er de kâns kriget. Men mat him sokke tiden hwat tasmite: in doek of in bal ofsa, dêr't er de tosken yn sette kin.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EDJSL012","role":"card","render":{"description":"A day labourer is returning home and sees a plough with no horse or man coming towards him. The plough changes shape: it is the smallholder, standing before him. The smallholder begs the man not to give him away.\nAt haymaking time the two men work together. When the smallholder is asleep, a mole comes out of his neck. The smallholder vomits litres of blood. In the meadow the remains of a calf are found; only a few gnawed bones are left. The smallholder dies. The priest has to come before the coffin can be carried to the churchyard.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1980,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9514","original":"Mol, de weerwolf\nEen keuterboer, die Mol heette, werd altijd uitgescholden:\n\"Bierpoep! Twee emmers vol snijbonen en nog maar wind!\"\nDat kwam omdat hij zoveel at.\nKarels, een dagloner, keerde 's avonds laat dwars door het veld terug naar huis, toen hij een ploeg zonder paard of man op zich af zag komen. Hij trok zijn mes, maar het ketste af op het ploegijzer. De ploeg veranderde van gedaante, en in de man die voor hem stond, herkende hij Mol.\nDeze viel op zijn knieën en smeekte hem niet te verraden. Hij zou Karels een mud boekweit en een mud rogge geven.\n\"Van jou, weerwolf, wil ik geen boekweit of rogge,\" zei de boerenknecht. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.3499,"rank":0.9535,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053702","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"Two men talking to each other find they have experienced the same thing: when they clung to a post during a boat trip at night, they touched a white figure. It is a ghostly apparition without a body. The figure then hurries along behind the hedge to the barn door.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25401","original":"Ik praette ris mei in keardel, dy sei: Dêr ha wy hwat bileefd! Wy wurken yn 'e polder. Mei de Feanster boat moest ik fuort by nacht. Ik moest troch hekken.\nIk wie by in hekke. Dêr wie in omstap neist. Ik krige de peal beet, doe taestte ik mei de hân op hwat.\n't Wie in gedaente yn 't wyt, dêr hie 'k op taest.\nFan kleare bare skrik haw ik der op houd mei de bôlleskeppe, dy't ik by my hie. Ik ha der gewoan trochhinne slein. Der siet gjin lichem oan. Doe bin 'k werom stapt.\nDe gedaente stapte achter de hage del en dy is ta de skûrdoar yn stapt.\nDoe't ik goed en wol op 'e boat wie, doe wie dêr ien op 'e boat, dy wie foar my itselde paed lâns kom.\nIk sil wol forbouwereard west ha en hwat wyt om 'e noas.\nDy oare sei tsjin my: \"Hwat sjochstû nuver. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ115905","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"At a certain place a gate keeps springing open: a ghost gate. Twelve men who take turns trying to push the gate shut at night see it spring open again every time. Someone was once murdered at that place. The ghost of the dead person still wanders about and keeps opening the gate.","place":"Eastermar","prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31213","original":"Op Bennema-state to Hurdegaryp stie de hekke altyd iepen. In kloftsje fan tolve man, dy kommen hjir út 'e omkriten wei, dy woenen dêr mear fan wite. Dy gongen dêr yn 'e nacht hinne en hâldden in weddenskip.\nIen foar ien dienen se de hekke ticht. Mar net sadra hie ien de hekke ticht dien of hy sprong direkt wer iepen. Deselde dy't it ús heit forteld hat wie ien fan 'e tolve. Hy wie de earste. As er de lêste west hie, sa fortelde er, dan hie er it net dwaen doarst. Sadra't er wer by de oare alve mannen stien hie wie de hekke samar út himsels tichtklapt.\nDêr moat ris ien formoarde woarn wêze. Dyselde fynt gjin rêst, en dwaelt dêr sûnt altyd om. Dan giet de hekke iepen, as er ticht is.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ081906","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"A peat skipper who is repeatedly startled by a naked little child behind his boat consults the minister. The minister asks the child, who died long ago, why it cannot find rest. It turns out the child drowned at that spot and was then buried without a shroud. The child asks the minister to request a burial shirt from the middle one of three women. The wish is granted and the minister hands the child the shroud with a wooden spoon. Now that its wish has been fulfilled, the child finds rest.","place":"Dokkum","prov":"Fr.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32618","original":"In Ternaard woonde in turfskipper. Alle kearen as dat skip daar lei dan kwam der in naken kiendsje achter bij 't skip op. De skipper wist niet hoe hij daar mee aan moest. Toen is hij naar doomny gaan en het hem fraagd wat dat was.\nDe doomny kwam op it skip en dy het bidden en hy het it kiend fraagd hwerom it geen rust hat.\nToen het dat kiend seid, hy had gjin bjirhemdtsje.\nHy was daar ferdronken en nu kon hy daar niet rusten.\nIt kiend sei: \"Over it pypke sullen drie dames lopen.\"\nDe middelste moesten se fragen om in bjirhemdsje.\nToen het de skipper henengaan en die het die middelste dame daar om fraagd. En hy het it kregen. En doe het er dat op it turfplak neergooid.\nEn doe het de doomny dat himdtsje dat kiend toereikt met een houten sleef. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058602","role":"inside","render":{"description":"The Jankemeer and the Trientsjemeer lie close to each other. A certain Janke drowned herself in the Jankemeer because her boyfriend had broken off their courtship. A certain Trientsje drowned in the Trientsjemeer. People heard noises then. A man with a white back in a waistcoat still haunts the place.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 2601","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26058","original":"By de Skieding hienen jo twa dobben. Oan 'e iene kant fan 'e wei wie de Janke-dobbe, oan 'e oare kant de Tryntsje-dobbe.\nDer wie in sekere Janke, dy hie in feint. Dy feint hie de forkearing mei har út makke, en doe hat Janke har dêr forsûpt. Sa hat dy dobbe de namme fan Janke-dobbe krigen. Sûnt hja har dêr forsûpt hat, spoeket it dêr.\nYn 'e oare dobbe ha se in sekere Tryntsje forsûpt. Tryntsje hat doe lûd jown. Letter hearden se dêr altyd lûden. In man mei in wite rêch yn 't festje spoeket dêr noch altyd om.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 2.","2 — 12 — 3."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"0eec280b8b12db04","accepted_hashes":["b7ab9fd4c8ff1ed4d0ab4cd52e3b8b134cc713e4947d72a6b44ab3103fbfb83b"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3555,"rank":1.0072,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ000413","role":"member","render":{"description":"A foal with a porridge pot around its neck does no one any harm.","place":"Nijega","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/11552","original":"Yn Aldegea roan in fôlle om mei in brijpot om 'e hals. Guon dy't de reden delgongen by de Opperbuorren ha him wol sjoen. Mar hy die net ien kwea.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ044202","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a certain spot a foal haunts with a porridge pot around its neck.","place":"De Tike","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24085","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ110804","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a horse roams about with a foal in its mouth. They are ghost animals.","place":"Opeinde","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29615","original":"Yn 'e Rottefalle spûke froeger in hynder mei in fôlle yn 'e bek. Der kaem dêr in famke út 'e jounsskoalle, dat fleach sûnder klompen oan nei hûs ta.\n\"Hwat skeelt dy?\" frege har heit.\n\"It hynder siet my achternei mei de fôlle yn 'e bek\", sei se. Dit is al hiel lang lyn.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ111716","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a large beast with glowing eyes roams about. You not only see the animal coming, you also hear it coming, because its feet sound like shod horses' hooves. When the animal approaches you must get away quickly, or else you will be thrown. The animal is the devil. If you throw the devil-beast a bread crust over your left shoulder, it goes away. Many night walkers carry a bread crust in their pocket.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29927","original":"Der spûke in swarte houn tusken Feankleaster en Twizel op it Wyldpaed. It wie in great beest, mei egen yn 'e kop as koallen fjûr. 't Waerd der ljocht fan yn 't tsjuster, as hy der oan kaem. Men koe him altyd oankommen hearre, hwant syn poaten klapten krekt as dy fan in hynder. Noait liker as sieten der hoefizers ûnder, sa hearde it.\nDer binne wol guon dy't him sjoen ha.\nKaem hy der oan, dan moesten se fan 'e wei gean, oars waerden se der wei smiten. It wie de duvel sels. As se him in breakoarste tasmieten oer 't linker skouder hinne, dan gong er fuort. De measte minsken hienen nachts as se der op út moesten, in breakoarste by har yn 'e bûse.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Kollumersweach belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2229,"rank":0.875,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ062011","role":"top","render":{"description":"Someone lives in Harkema, and when he comes back late from the farmer's he always meets an old woman on the path, whom he greets.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26947","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP263","role":"half","render":{"description":"He says the little brother must ask the ghost what is wrong. The answer is that the young man died twenty-five years too early because of the stabbing. His soul must keep haunting all those years until the time is up. The priest orders the ghost to be shut in a separate room that may not be opened for the next twenty-five years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ109412","role":"half","render":{"description":"The minister opens the Bible and lays a key of the house on a certain text. The next morning the key has turned towards the apple tree. A murdered child turns out to be buried there. After the child is reburied in the churchyard, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ030711","role":"half","render":{"description":"One of the family members is once offered a hand out of nowhere. The barn doors also blow open by themselves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KEMP181","role":"half","render":{"description":"The body parts come together and form an old man. It is a ghost that keeps giving the soldier orders: that he must go to the cellar and lift a stone, and so on. The man boldly refuses and makes the ghost do everything itself. Three pots of gold turn out to be hidden in the farmstead. The spirit tells the soldier to give one pot to the church and one to the poor, and he may keep one himself, as thanks for releasing the ghost, who had been wicked in his life and exploited the poor.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0111","role":"half","render":{"description":"Asked why it appears, the shade answers that he is her father and can only enter heaven once three more Masses have been said. After the girl has done this, her health improves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ062011","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"She is always sweeping the path and the yard with a broom. One evening at full moon he sees the old woman standing in the yard again, leaning on her broom, although she has been dead for four months.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450","stain":"four"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘woman’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0450. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c7","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c7"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1","word":"four","stained":"c7"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
